I was recently thinking about the design of nethack and trying to get
myself into the 'dev-team' mood for a simple mod, having been hacking
around with the source quite a bit for a more difficult modification I
am feasibility testing.
It has to be seem incredibly useful at first but be balanced by
creating tons of opportunities for YASD.
Suddenly, I thought of a truly Useful/Fiendishly Evil item.

Boots of Disintigration.

Since it is actually quite far away from the simple mod I was
brainstorming for I will post it here and get some comments.
----

So here goes an exercise in balancing useful / evil features of an
item:

Boots of Disintigration;
spiked leather boots
enchant 1d6 - 2
cursed 2:3 times

Effects:

Any time an effect is activated the boots have a chance of re-cursing
themselves. 'boots feel like they are melding into your slowly
dissolving skin'. 1:10 blessed 1:5 uncursed. 33% chance of resisting
removal and recursing.

Stepping on items destroys 1d3 - 1 items on the floor
Walking on drawbridge destroys bridge, trapdoors are turned into holes
(and you fall)
Kick zaps disintigrate, chance of instakill would be lowered.
Kick always destroys doors.
Kick sink causes flooding
Falling into spike pit shatters spikes.
Stepping on a fountain causes flooding.
kicking a chest destroys it and disintigrates most of the items
Destroy spider webs, some traps
Destroy engravings
Never stuck in lava, but still damaged
Shatters ice; 'cracks appear under your feet, you'd better move fast'
Punishment, Ball and chain, 'chain rattles into pieces'
Stepping in monster corpses can get their juices on you. Good for YASD.

#jump can cause earthquake or mass disintigration, 1:5 (earth) or 1:3
same as breaking digging. 'The dungeon disintigrates around you'

You cannot enter a shop with them on. Shop keepers are not stupid.

Kicking a wall can
1:10 same as breaking a wand of digging 'The dungeon disintigrates
around you'
3:10 nothing, you gouge the wall
1:10 you destroy the wall and cause a cavein as per scroll of earth
5:10 destroy the wall.

Altars -
step on a coaligned alter will uncurse the boots if not chaotic and in
favor with your god.
'Your god calms the chaos' only happens once for each prayer timeout
otherwise if chaotic nothing, you 'feel the earth shake'
otherwise luck -5, you hear the alter crackling, you have a premonition
of dread.

Although this is a very bad item it is also a very useful item. Maybe
too useful if you can write remove curse and don't really need any more
items from the floor to ascend.

